Article 18 The State may, on any of the following grounds, prohibit or restrict the import or export of relevant goods or technologies, or take other necessary measures:
(1) to safeguard national security, public interests, or public morals;
(2) to protect human health or safety, the life or health of animals or plants, or the environment;
(3) to implement measures relating to the import or export of gold or silver;
(4) shortage of domestic supply or for the effective protection of natural resources that may be exhausted;
(5) limited market capacity in the importing country or region;
(6) serious disorder in export order;
(7) to establish or accelerate the establishment of a specific domestic industry;
(8) necessary restrictions on the import of agricultural, animal husbandry, or fishery products in any form;
(9) to safeguard the international financial status of the State and its balance of international payments;
(10) where, in accordance with the provisions of laws or administrative regulations, it is necessary to prohibit or restrict the import or export of relevant goods or technologies, or to take other necessary measures;
(11) where, in accordance with the provisions of international treaties or agreements concluded or acceded to by the People's Republic of China, it is necessary to prohibit or restrict the import or export of relevant goods or technologies, or to take other necessary measures;
(12) other circumstances where it is necessary to prohibit or restrict the import or export of relevant goods or technologies, or to take other necessary measures.

Article 29 The State may, on any of the following grounds, prohibit or restrict the relevant international service trade, or take other necessary measures:
(1) for the purpose of safeguarding national security, social public interests or public morality;
(2) for the purpose of protecting human health or safety, protecting the life or health of animals or plants, or protecting the environment;
(3) for the purpose of establishing or accelerating the establishment of a specific domestic service industry;
(4) for the purpose of ensuring the balance of international payments of the State;
(5) where other prohibitions or restrictions on the relevant international service trade or other necessary measures are required in accordance with the provisions of laws and administrative regulations;
(6) where other prohibitions or restrictions on the relevant international service trade or other necessary measures are required under the provisions of international treaties or agreements concluded or acceded to by the People's Republic of China;
(7) where other prohibitions or restrictions on the relevant international service trade or other necessary measures are required.

Article 37 In foreign trade activities, no one shall commit any of the following acts:
(1) forging or altering marks of origin of imported or exported goods, forging, altering or buying or selling certificates of origin, import and export quota certificates, import and export licenses, tariff quota certificates or other import or export certification documents;
(2) evading the payment of domestic taxes due on exports, or fraudulently obtaining export tax refunds;
(3) engaging in smuggling;
(4) evading the certification, inspection or quarantine required by laws or administrative regulations;
(5) committing other acts that violate the provisions of laws or administrative regulations.

Article 40 The competent foreign trade department of the State Council may take measures such as prohibiting or restricting the import or export of goods and technologies, and international service trade related to the People's Republic of China, against any foreign individual or organization under any of the following circumstances:
(1) endangering the sovereignty, security or development interests of the People's Republic of China;
(2) violating normal market transaction principles, suspending normal transactions with individuals or organizations of the People's Republic of China, and seriously harming the legitimate rights and interests of individuals or organizations of the People's Republic of China;
(3) adopting discriminatory measures against individuals or organizations of the People's Republic of China, and seriously harming the legitimate rights and interests of individuals or organizations of the People's Republic of China.
No individual or organization shall provide support, assistance or facilitation such as agency, freight, delivery, customs declaration, warehousing or third-party trading platform services for the purpose of evading the measures specified in the preceding paragraph.

Article 41 For the purpose of maintaining the order of foreign trade, the competent department of foreign trade under the State Council may, on its own or jointly with other relevant departments under the State Council, investigate the following matters in accordance with the provisions of laws and administrative regulations:
(1) the impact of import and export of goods, import and export of technologies, and international service trade on domestic industries and their competitiveness;
(2) trade-related barriers of relevant countries or regions;
(3) matters that need to be investigated to determine whether anti-dumping, countervailing or safeguard measures and other foreign trade remedy measures shall be taken according to law;
(4) acts of evading foreign trade remedy measures;
(5) matters concerning national security interests in foreign trade;
(6) matters that need to be investigated for the implementation of the provisions of Article 10, paragraph 2 of Article 32, Article 34, and Article 35 of this Law;
(7) other matters affecting the order of foreign trade that need to be investigated.
